Ours, not upstream (also in PoissonRecon master and COLMAP main as of
2026-10): give the Poisson mesher's polygon centre vertices a defined value.

When a polygon of the extracted iso-surface is split into triangles around
its centre, AddIsoPolygons starts the centre vertex as `Vertex c; c *= 0;`.
The position is zeroed by its constructor, but the density value isn't
initialised, and stack garbage times 0 is NaN when the garbage is NaN or
infinite. -ffast-math, which COLMAP uses everywhere but MSVC, folds x*0 to 0
and hides it; clang without it (clang-cl on Windows, or plain clang -O2)
writes NaN densities, and the surface trimmer then turns every vertex it
interpolates from them into NaN (seen as test_poisson_onsphere_splats
failing). Starting from the first corner gives the same mean without the
uninitialised read.

diff --git a/src/thirdparty/PoissonRecon/FEMTree.LevelSet.3D.inl b/src/thirdparty/PoissonRecon/FEMTree.LevelSet.3D.inl
index 50c85b0..0253d87 100644
--- a/src/thirdparty/PoissonRecon/FEMTree.LevelSet.3D.inl
+++ b/src/thirdparty/PoissonRecon/FEMTree.LevelSet.3D.inl
@@ -1924,9 +1924,8 @@ public:
 					}
 			if( isCoplanar )
 			{
-				Vertex c;
-				c *= 0;
-				for( unsigned int i=0 ; i<polygon.size() ; i++ ) c += polygon[i].second;
+				Vertex c = polygon[0].second;
+				for( unsigned int i=1 ; i<polygon.size() ; i++ ) c += polygon[i].second;
 				c /= ( typename Vertex::Real )polygon.size();
 
 				node_index_type cIdx = (node_index_type)vertexStream.write( thread , c );
